       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg per day. That's twice the usual maximum of about 2,550 mg per day (2,000\u20132,550 mg depending on the formulation). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850\u20131,000 mg per dose. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg per day and the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first, and I'll enter it only after that."
      }
